# A register clocked by a clock the job never declares carries NO check.
#
# OpenSTA seeds clock-tagged paths only at pins the SDC names as a clock source, so
# pclk_i here is an ordinary data input: its arrival propagates through b1/b2 as DATA
# and r2's CLK pin never holds a clock. VisitPathEnds::visitCheckEnd then builds no
# PathEndCheck for r2 at all -- it is an unconstrained endpoint, not a passing one.
#
# input_delay is declared (12 ns, as fft_top's SDC does) precisely so this cannot be
# confused with the unconstrained-INPUT-PORT rule: every port here has an arrival, and
# r2 must still go unchecked because its CLOCK is undeclared.
# OUT OF SCOPE, deliberately left in: r2/Q still launches a path into the constrained
# output pq_o, so the golden shows a setup violation there. That is not a defect of this
# rule -- OpenSTA's arrival search crosses a reg CLK->Q arc too (`SearchPred2::searchThru`
# blocks only timing-check edges), so the path genuinely exists. The rule declines the
# four REGISTER checks, which is what was specified and measured; the output-delay side
# is a separate question and is not claimed here.
design:      undeclared_clk
netlist:     undeclared_clk.v
lib:         undeclared_clk.lib
clock:       clk_i clk_i 2.0
input_slew:  0.02
output_load: 0.005
input_delay: 12.0
